# `yo fix <path> --migrate explicit-copy --hot-path <path>` lists the copies
# in a file under a hot path for a hand edit instead of cloning them: a deep
# copy per operation compounds there, and the edit is usually a borrow or a
# share (plans/VALUES_BY_DEFAULT.md B1, "Path to a landable B1": the parked
# sweep's ~3,100 src/ clones, 1,268 of them in src/evaluator/, measured
# ~80-100x slower). The same copy shape outside the hot path (`b := a` in
# main.yo) is still rewritten, so the guard is scoped to the path,
# segment-wise. The copies are of a `BTreeMap` (still a `ref`; decision
# Option 1 of issues/questions/2026-10-27-what-the-implicit-copy-audit-and-the-explicit-copy-migration-cover-after-b8.md).
# The expected_tree pins main.yo rewritten and hot/engine.yo unchanged; the
# trailing `check` proves the result still evaluates.
stdout_keep=^fix:
timeout=240
